 ## Overview
-The SOG Volume Reader is a recursive algorithm that loads a hierarchical volumetric format (SOG) into a dense 3D grid by parsing a binary header and traversing internal, empty, leaf, and pseudo-leaf node types [S1, S2, unofficial]. It differs from flat raw readers by reconstructing the full voxel array from a compressed octree-like structure, enabling efficient storage of sparse or block-structured medical imaging data [S1, S2, unofficial].
